    "font-color-white": "text-color-white",
    "text-bold": "text-weight-700",
    "heading-31-3": "heading-43-3"
  },
  "notes": {
    ".p1": "a class literally named .p1 (an importer artefact), 1.125rem lead paragraph size",
    "p3": "The 4 fit-checklist item texts (1rem at every width). Its declarations equal text-size-regular at base, but text-size-regular also sets 1.148rem on mobile, so a merge would move them. A utility-shaped name (text-size-regular-fixed) fails class-audit --strict as a reimplemented utility; a custom folder_element class holding one utility's declarations is allowed (CLASS-STANDARD section 5), so it is named for its element. Whether these 4 paragraphs should take the mobile bump and merge into text-size-regular is a separate visual decision.",
    "kicker": "the tagline role (Client-First text-style-tagline); it also carries colour and margin",
    "eyebrow": "tagline in a bordered pill; 'eyebrow' is out of bounds per CLASS-STANDARD.md",
    "text-lh-*": "line-height utilities, named from their value: text-style-line-height-1-7 = 1.7",
    "text-tracking-*": "letter-spacing utilities named from their em value: text-style-letter-spacing-minus-0-04 = -0.04em",
    "text-NN-MM": "responsive font-size fragments from the 2026-09-15 type-roles pass; renamed text-size-custom-NN-MM, folding them into the role classes is a separate visual decision",
    "-alternate": "converter context variants (parent_child) of a class with different declarations; the variant takes -alternate",
    "hc": "hero carousel (data-hero-carousel)",
    "cs": "customer story",
    "v5/v2": "version prefixes dropped",
    "generated": "399 Framework-generated colour utilities (bg-*, border-*, text-*-d-1 …) are left alone: the Framework owns and regenerates them",
    "heading-31-3": "identical to heading-43-3; merged (engine supports merging into a renamed class since 2026-10-05)",
    "merges": "font-weight-600 = text-weight-600, text-bold = text-weight-700 (then renamed to the library text-weight-semibold/bold), font-color-white = text-color-white, active = is-active (both empty rules; the script toggles it)",
    "result": "NOT IN MAP (yet): site.js does chart.querySelector('.grow-bar.result'); class-rename.mjs rewriteJs skips a class preceded by a word char (treats '.result' in '.grow-bar.result' as a property access), so renaming would leave the script on the old name and break the result-lab chart. Intended name: bar-track_result. Add it back once the engine rewrites compound selectors."
  }
}